  "grammarTip": "The dative case marks the indirect object — the person 'to' or 'for' whom something happens — and follows verbs like reći, dati, pomoći, and pisati. Masculine nouns add -u (šef → šefu), nouns ending in -a like kolega/kolegica change to -i (kolega → kolegi, kolegica → kolegici), and neuter nouns add -u (dijete → djetetu). 'Pomogao sam kolegici sa izvještajem' — I helped my colleague (f.) with the report.",
